Let $n$ be the number of sides of the polygon.  The sum of the interior angles of an $n$-sided polygon is $(n-2) \cdot 180$ degrees.  Since one of the interior angles is 160 degrees and the rest are 112 degrees, we have
\[(n-2) \cdot 180 = 160 + 112(n-1).\]Solving for $n$, we get $n = 10$.

\boxed{10}

